  "body_html": "<p></p><p>Please note before reading, these company reviews are my analysis and opinions. Also note, that just because I say something looks bullish does not mean I go buying all the time. I do these as a courtesy for all of you, as a 2nd opinion. If I bought every single thing I reviewed, that was bullish, I would have a portfolio with way too many tickers to track. Additionally, about 95% of my own trades are strictly VCP breakouts. </p><div><hr></div><h4>Archrock, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$AROC&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> - Natural Gas Compression Services &amp; Equipment</h4><p><strong>StockTok’s Verdict:</strong></p><ul><li><p>If you are up &gt;10%, DCA up (beware earnings later today)</p></li><li><p>If you are not in it, avoid</p></li></ul><p>Though I do not think AROC is a great <em><strong>initial investment</strong></em> right now, as the main SEPA (specific entry point analysis) entry occurred on 21 January (or 05 February depending on strategy preference for macro breakouts), it is at a great spot to add to current positions. I know you may scratch your head and say “if its good too add to a position, why not buy an initial?!”  You would likely be fine with an initial position, as trend is friend, but the key difference, is someone adding to a position can risk profits, not portfolio equity. We want optimal conditions for initial entries. </p><p>If you are still having trouble spotting volatility contraction patterns (VCPs), this is an outstanding hindsight example to train your eyes. Notice that the stock is in a macro uptrend and forms a flag pole and then several higher lows with a relatively flat price ceiling (yellow lines). Then the initial breakout from the consolidation occurred on 21 January, with above average volume. Volume does not have to be the LARGEST, but it does need to be above average. That gap up is even better corroboration of a breakout. This would be the optimal spot for a SEPA entry (I wish I had seen this a few months ago). As price broke above the local high, at ~$30, this would also be a good SEPA entry, or DCA up, if you are more of a ATH momentum breakout trader. Either is fine, just be consistent. The recent break out from the local consolidation between ~$34 - ~$37 would be another great DCA up spot. Compound your winners, not your losers.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"673\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:673,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:227438,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196545679?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pKLr!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3c10387e-142f-4b8a-a7bc-e67676f211a8_1766x816.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Fundamentals are fine with both cash flow and EPS improving annually. </p><p>My forecast is for continued upward price action…the primary reason I will NOT buy though, is the SEPA entries have passed, and it is total guessing how high it will go. I cannot secure profits first. Also, be aware earnings is later today for AROC…I don’t mess with earnings when mid-term investing unless I am in &gt;20% profit. </p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div><hr></div><h4>Vertiv Holdings, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$VRT&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>  - Digital Infrastructure</h4><p><strong>StockTok’s Verdict</strong></p><ul><li><p>Buy</p></li></ul><p>VRT has an incredibly strong trend, all the way back to 2022. What is even more impressive is the massive cash flow growth. In 2020, the company had a 1,561% growth in cash flow. And that trend continued to even last year, with a 64% growth. Through February, March and April, when most of the market was in decline, VRT continued pushing upwards. Even on 20 March, when sellers aggressively sold off, the price action barely budged, indicating that the bulls remain in control and buying was eating up the selling action. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png\" width=\"1374\" height=\"823\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:823,&quot;width&quot;:1374,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:135107,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196545679?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ygau!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17513d3d-7f13-45c4-95d9-f735a280c054_1374x823.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>I prefer a breakout from VCP pattern personally, but there is no indication that the trend is over for VRT. Forecast remains bullish. </p><div><hr></div><h4>Sterling Infrastructure, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$STRL&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> - E-Infrastructure  </h4><p>StockTok’s Verdict</p><ul><li><p>Very Risky</p></li></ul><p>STRL pumped over 43% today, after an earnings beat. Those beats are based off “analysts expectations.” Most Wall Street analysts are absolutely worthless…so I never really care what their expectations or projections are. If they were Market Wizards, they wouldn’t be sitting in an office writing expectations at all. Harsh truth. </p><p>When we look closer though at actual earnings, I question what is going on. Looking at Q126, cash flow beat “analyst’s 🤡 expectations”…but actually declined from the prior quarter, from $159M to $145M. It’s even worse on the annual timeframe, going from $416M to $361M. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><div class=\"image-link image2\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png\" width=\"1424\" height=\"60\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:60,&quot;width&quot;:1424,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:8325,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196545679?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVNZ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F734012f8-31b0-458f-9be6-9db2a61e270e_1424x60.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div></div></div></div></figure></div><p>Because of this, that gap up, from earnings, makes me question the longevity of the rise. Can it continue? Is it likely to continue? Or will the gap fill? Those questions of uncertainty push me to say “no thank you” as I prefer higher probability odds of both short term, and long term, success. I prefer when we have a combination of both chart technicals and fundamental reasoning, and here, it seems to just be a catalyst driven event. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xSMS!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc77b9a49-78bf-4db5-abd5-3e6f3c4105a4_1368x822.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xSMS!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc77b9a49-78bf-4db5-abd5-3e6f3c4105a4_1368x822.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xSMS!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc77b9a49-78bf-4db5-abd5-3e6f3c4105a4_1368x822.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xSMS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc77b9a49-78bf-4db5-abd5-3e6f3c4105a4_1368x822.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xSMS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc77b9a49-78bf-4db5-abd5-3e6f3c4105a4_1368x822.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xSMS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:s